    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0575" n="471" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg471"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.001 P69/3.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President to the Constitutional President of Ecuador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The White House</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-01-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 10, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Great and Good Friend</hi>: I have received your
                    letter of the 20th of September last<anchor n="1" xml:id="d506-f1"/>, in which
                    Your Excellency announced your assumption, on the 30th<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d506-f2"/> of August last, of the Presidency of the Republic of
                    Ecuador.</p>
                <p>I cordially reciprocate the sentiments you express for the continuance of the
                    friendly relations which have heretofore existed between the United States and
                    Ecuador, and I assure Your Excellency of my best wishes for your personal
                    welfare and for the prosperity of the Republic over which you have been called
                    upon to preside.</p>
                <p>Your Good Friend,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. H. Taft</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
